WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.080 --> 00:03.650
[This series contains scenes of violence, self-harm, and potential triggers.]

3
00:03.650 --> 00:05.230
[Viewer discretion is advised.]

4
00:14.230 --> 00:15.660
What are you doing?

5
00:20.620 --> 00:21.730
You said the meds were bitter.

6
00:21.730 --> 00:23.270
What the hell is all this?

7
00:23.470 --> 00:25.410
You forced me to sing,

8
00:25.560 --> 00:26.980
to join the audition,

9
00:27.460 --> 00:28.660
eliminated me,

10
00:29.650 --> 00:31.160
and now this.

11
00:34.570 --> 00:36.470
What do you want from me?

12
00:39.550 --> 00:40.660
Tell me.

13
00:42.160 --> 00:43.440
Your voice.

14
00:44.930 --> 00:46.930
As a songwriter, I covet your voice.

15
00:48.100 --> 00:51.540
I want you to sing only my songs,

16
00:52.010 --> 00:53.020
Lee Hanyul.

17
00:57.230 --> 00:58.760
Isn't it a blessing for you?

18
01:00.210 --> 01:03.470
Singers are lined up out the door, begging to sing my songs.

19
01:08.110 --> 01:09.640
As long as you keep your word

20
01:10.750 --> 01:13.010
about getting Adolph's song back for me,

21
01:14.180 --> 01:15.830
I'll do anything.

22
01:16.130 --> 01:17.250
But...

23
01:18.900 --> 01:20.430
don't cross the line again.

24
01:21.010 --> 01:22.630
Apart from my voice,

25
01:23.560 --> 01:25.100
leave me alone.

26
01:30.000 --> 01:31.320
You're all the same.

27
01:33.030 --> 01:34.479
You selfishly chase

28
01:36.500 --> 01:40.030
whatever you want with zero regard for anyone else's feelings.

29
01:47.009 --> 01:48.220
Don't touch me.

30
02:00.940 --> 02:07.620
[Some scenes were created with AI.]

31
02:09.840 --> 02:13.530
[Adapted from the webtoon "The Sound of Sugar Cubes" by Kim Tak]

32
02:13.540 --> 02:16.300
[Screenwriter: So-on (JD)]

33
02:16.360 --> 02:19.290
[Director: Yoon Jinyoung]

34
02:35.760 --> 02:37.290
[Yoo Dohyun]

35
02:37.400 --> 02:38.960
[Cho Chanhyeon]

36
02:39.079 --> 02:40.600
[Ko Gyeol]

37
02:42.090 --> 02:45.600
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

38
02:51.970 --> 02:53.060
Lee Hanyul,

39
02:53.960 --> 02:56.970
I want you to sing only for me.

40
02:59.390 --> 03:00.710
You have no idea

41
03:01.550 --> 03:03.090
how intoxicating

42
03:03.370 --> 03:05.330
your voice is.

43
03:21.260 --> 03:22.690
You selfishly chase

44
03:23.329 --> 03:26.860
whatever you want with zero regard for anyone else's feelings.

45
03:41.240 --> 03:45.550
Dawn always comes softly,

46
03:45.680 --> 03:49.600
leaving secret tears behind.

47
03:49.740 --> 03:51.620
The streets without you,

48
03:51.760 --> 03:53.630
the breeze without you—

49
03:53.770 --> 03:58.100
why does this night seem endless?

50
03:58.240 --> 04:01.960
Just once, just this once—

51
04:02.150 --> 04:04.010
if I could...

52
05:12.660 --> 05:14.120
Are you feeling better?

53
05:15.080 --> 05:18.220
My voice is.

54
05:18.690 --> 05:19.890
That's what matters.

55
05:19.930 --> 05:21.200
Get ready and come out.

56
05:21.930 --> 05:23.210
Why should I?

57
05:25.260 --> 05:27.500
We have to get on with our business.

58
05:28.470 --> 05:30.400
Our needs are very clear:

59
05:30.830 --> 05:32.470
you want Adolph's song,

60
05:32.630 --> 05:34.040
and I want your voice.

61
05:34.159 --> 05:36.680
This is business to satisfy

62
05:36.930 --> 05:38.130
our mutual needs.

63
05:39.880 --> 05:41.440
You're really annoying.

64
05:42.610 --> 05:43.330
I know.

65
05:43.470 --> 05:44.390
Go get ready.

66
05:44.510 --> 05:45.450
Wait here.

67
05:56.210 --> 05:59.510
[Pack all his stuff.]

68
06:03.850 --> 06:05.140
Where are we?

69
06:06.020 --> 06:07.590
To meet someone.

70
06:07.880 --> 06:09.020
Who?

71
06:09.500 --> 06:10.790
Your vocal coach.

72
06:14.690 --> 06:15.760
What's wrong?

73
06:16.720 --> 06:18.820
I'm... broke.

74
06:20.330 --> 06:21.810
I'll pay for it.

75
06:22.200 --> 06:23.340
Why would you?

76
06:24.430 --> 06:25.560
It's an investment.

77
06:25.740 --> 06:26.700
No.

78
06:27.500 --> 06:30.630
You'll just use that as an excuse to cross the line again.

79
06:30.950 --> 06:33.480
Then consider it... a loan.

80
06:33.620 --> 06:35.100
Same difference.

81
06:35.420 --> 06:37.460
Just think of it as borrowed money.

82
06:38.560 --> 06:39.820
But the collateral...

83
06:39.940 --> 06:41.390
My voice.

84
06:41.800 --> 06:43.580
It's my voice and nothing more.

85
06:43.900 --> 06:45.100
Then the interest...

86
06:45.100 --> 06:46.250
What interest?

87
06:46.810 --> 06:47.720
Wake-up calls.

88
06:47.830 --> 06:49.030
No way.

89
06:50.190 --> 06:51.420
Then we have a deal.

90
06:51.540 --> 06:52.750
I didn't agree.

91
06:54.690 --> 06:56.050
By the way...

92
06:59.510 --> 07:01.580
are you into men or women?

93
07:03.980 --> 07:06.190
M... Men?

94
07:07.450 --> 07:09.570
Or is anyone fine for you?

95
07:10.130 --> 07:11.320
Hey.

96
07:13.410 --> 07:15.070
Why are you asking me this?

97
07:18.010 --> 07:19.650
Is it that Herod?

98
07:28.800 --> 07:30.250
I knew it.

99
07:34.860 --> 07:36.050
But does he even

100
07:37.409 --> 07:39.340
know where he's going?

101
07:44.270 --> 07:45.960
Once I get the song back,

102
07:46.760 --> 07:48.300
we're done.

103
07:55.560 --> 07:56.850
It's me, Pan.

104
08:00.050 --> 08:01.400
Yo, Lee Won!

105
08:04.160 --> 08:05.760
Who's that cutie next to you?

106
08:05.810 --> 08:06.760
Your boyfriend?

107
08:06.770 --> 08:07.460
Huh?

108
08:07.600 --> 08:09.330
No! What are you talking about?

109
08:09.610 --> 08:10.660
Absolutely not.

110
08:11.150 --> 08:11.980
Right?

111
08:12.140 --> 08:15.580
How could a monster like you have such a cute boyfriend?

112
08:15.720 --> 08:17.310
Then...

113
08:17.310 --> 08:18.900
can I have him?

114
08:23.210 --> 08:24.210
Okay, okay.

115
08:24.410 --> 08:25.500
Got it.

116
08:26.190 --> 08:27.450
What's your name?

117
08:27.560 --> 08:28.960
I'm Lee Hanyul.

118
08:29.210 --> 08:30.540
Hanyul Lee?

119
08:30.660 --> 08:33.360
Okay, show me what you've got.

120
08:38.960 --> 08:44.130
Today, I make my way across the dawn

121
08:45.000 --> 08:51.340
to call out to you once more.

122
08:54.710 --> 08:56.100
Whoa.

123
08:56.800 --> 08:58.040
Whoa.

124
08:58.280 --> 08:59.570
What's with you?

125
08:59.630 --> 09:02.600
Holy, what a find this time.

126
09:02.880 --> 09:05.470
No wonder you're so obsessed with him.

127
09:05.730 --> 09:06.640
Hah.

128
09:08.980 --> 09:09.960
Come on.

129
09:11.400 --> 09:13.080
Let me formally introduce myself.

130
09:13.080 --> 09:14.270
I'm your mentor,

131
09:14.520 --> 09:16.210
Pan.

132
09:16.500 --> 09:19.500
I've finally found the perfect protégé I've been looking for.

133
09:19.500 --> 09:23.380
You... You don't know how long I've waited for you.

134
09:23.400 --> 09:25.240
-I've waited my whole life for you... -Enough.

135
09:25.240 --> 09:26.850
Enough. Cut it out!

136
09:27.270 --> 09:28.390
Come with me.

137
09:38.220 --> 09:39.100
Damn it.

138
09:39.640 --> 09:40.700
Damn it.

139
09:44.900 --> 09:46.710
About ten years ago,

140
09:47.780 --> 09:50.440
he was the lead singer of a popular group abroad.

141
09:51.130 --> 09:53.190
"Was"?

142
09:53.470 --> 09:54.930
Ask him yourself later on.

143
09:57.480 --> 09:59.480
Anyway, you'll learn a lot from him.

144
10:00.610 --> 10:04.340
He's the perfect mentor for a runaway like you.

145
10:06.030 --> 10:07.720
Ah, so sad.

146
10:12.530 --> 10:15.810
Goodness, stop eating those cup noodles already.

147
10:16.140 --> 10:17.470
Ugh, they're all soggy.

148
10:17.990 --> 10:19.790
Hey, let's start training.

149
10:19.990 --> 10:21.670
And you can go now.

150
10:22.920 --> 10:24.450
I was about to leave anyway.

151
10:34.600 --> 10:36.200
Secretary Han, you're here.

152
10:37.230 --> 10:38.390
What's all that?

153
10:38.950 --> 10:39.940
Luggage.

154
10:40.130 --> 10:41.260
Whose luggage?

155
10:42.630 --> 10:43.640
What?

156
10:53.410 --> 10:56.040
I told you not to cross the line, didn't I?

157
10:56.300 --> 10:57.270
Hmm?

158
10:57.770 --> 10:58.990
It wasn't me.

159
10:59.550 --> 11:00.900
He did it.

160
11:03.500 --> 11:05.110
Your house is put up for rent.

161
11:05.340 --> 11:06.610
What?

162
11:06.870 --> 11:08.520
It's all or nothing.

163
11:08.640 --> 11:11.370
You don't have time to go back and forth every day.

164
11:18.170 --> 11:19.970
This is your training schedule.

165
11:20.910 --> 11:22.110
I'll leave him to you.

166
11:24.680 --> 11:25.790
Hey!

167
11:25.920 --> 11:26.990
Lee Won!

168
11:32.800 --> 11:34.300
[Monday: Exercise, English Lesson, Lunch, Rap Lesson, Self-study, Dinner,]

169
11:34.300 --> 11:35.140
[Weekly Evaluation, Dance Lesson]

170
11:39.530 --> 11:43.570
What does a songwriter know about vocals?

171
11:43.840 --> 11:45.050
He's so full of himself.

172
11:45.050 --> 11:46.110
Buzz off, you brat!

173
11:46.140 --> 11:47.550
Go to hell.

174
11:48.200 --> 11:49.390
You...

175
11:50.850 --> 11:52.510
Just trust me.

176
11:53.730 --> 11:54.530
That's it.

177
11:54.780 --> 11:56.360
That cheeky snob.

178
11:58.280 --> 12:02.240
[Training 1: Hide Your Breath]

179
11:58.910 --> 12:00.440
Okay, now we are

180
12:00.980 --> 12:02.730
going to play hide-and-seek.

181
12:03.010 --> 12:04.610
Eh? Hide-and-seek?

182
12:04.730 --> 12:05.550
Yeah.

183
12:06.330 --> 12:07.320
Just the two of us?

184
12:07.320 --> 12:08.850
Come on! Rock, paper...

185
12:09.270 --> 12:10.210
scissors!

186
12:10.220 --> 12:12.050
Jeez, I won.

187
12:12.190 --> 12:13.250
I'll be the seeker.

188
12:13.320 --> 12:14.900
Why are you the seeker when you won?

189
12:14.900 --> 12:16.260
I'll count to five.

190
12:16.810 --> 12:17.740
What?

191
12:18.520 --> 12:19.310
One!

192
12:19.490 --> 12:20.300
Two!

193
12:20.490 --> 12:21.270
Three!

194
12:21.450 --> 12:22.300
Four!

195
12:22.460 --> 12:23.480
Five!

196
12:25.060 --> 12:26.490
Gotcha!

197
12:29.800 --> 12:31.010
Gotcha!

198
12:34.200 --> 12:35.520
Gotcha!

199
12:35.840 --> 12:36.870
Mr. Pan,

200
12:37.000 --> 12:38.650
how do you keep finding me so easily?

201
12:38.650 --> 12:40.350
I didn't even make a peep.

202
12:41.520 --> 12:43.220
I didn't hear your voice,

203
12:43.360 --> 12:45.630
but I heard your breath.

204
12:45.910 --> 12:47.210
My breath?

205
12:47.830 --> 12:49.700
But I was holding my breath.

206
12:50.180 --> 12:55.280
Hey, holding your breath... will kill you.

207
12:55.400 --> 12:57.200
You're still alive, aren't you?

208
12:58.190 --> 13:02.150
A ragged breath, frozen in terror— afraid of being found.

209
13:02.410 --> 13:04.610
You can't hide the sound of being alive.

210
13:05.250 --> 13:08.170
A lot is revealed through your voice:

211
13:08.300 --> 13:09.300
your tone,

212
13:09.420 --> 13:10.500
your mood,

213
13:10.630 --> 13:11.880
and your breath.

214
13:11.950 --> 13:14.010
Things you can't hide even if you try.

215
13:14.850 --> 13:16.590
Wow, that was poetic.

216
13:17.420 --> 13:21.580
So don't run away trying to hide it half-heartedly.

217
13:21.590 --> 13:23.190
There's no hiding it anyway.

218
13:23.240 --> 13:24.490
Okay?

219
13:24.880 --> 13:26.330
Let's move on to the next stage!

220
13:26.330 --> 13:27.170
Let's go.

221
13:29.330 --> 13:30.320
I'm okay.

222
13:30.440 --> 13:31.540
I'm fine.

223
13:34.890 --> 13:38.560
[Training 2: Fight Against the Wind]

224
13:37.800 --> 13:38.860
It's hot, isn't it?

225
13:40.100 --> 13:41.310
Stage two:

226
13:41.720 --> 13:46.310
fighting against the wind...

227
13:46.740 --> 13:48.520
Against...

228
13:48.650 --> 13:49.410
No.

229
13:49.590 --> 13:52.760
Against the wind...

230
13:53.310 --> 13:55.130
By the way, how does this help?

231
13:55.960 --> 13:57.400
When you stand on stage,

232
13:57.650 --> 14:00.310
all sorts of things will come riding on the wind.

233
14:00.400 --> 14:01.750
What kind of things?

234
14:02.190 --> 14:02.980
Gazes,

235
14:03.160 --> 14:03.830
memories,

236
14:03.990 --> 14:05.080
and regrets.

237
14:05.300 --> 14:06.560
You must have them too.

238
14:06.810 --> 14:08.330
Memories that bring you regret,

239
14:08.330 --> 14:11.070
someone's gaze that you can never erase.

240
14:12.310 --> 14:14.700
In that moment, your whole body will stiffen,

241
14:14.700 --> 14:16.330
and so will your throat.

242
14:16.500 --> 14:19.380
Come out! Ah!

243
14:21.050 --> 14:25.000
There's no such thing as lasting peace anyway.

244
14:25.000 --> 14:28.450
We just briefly delude ourselves into believing things have improved.

245
14:28.450 --> 14:29.810
Because

246
14:30.460 --> 14:32.540
the wind...

247
14:32.540 --> 14:34.630
will keep blowing!

248
14:34.810 --> 14:36.400
Ah!

249
14:36.700 --> 14:38.920
You try it too! "Ah"!

250
14:39.210 --> 14:40.310
Ah...

251
14:40.440 --> 14:41.610
Louder!

252
14:41.780 --> 14:44.580
-Ah! -Ah! Good! Now try singing!

253
14:44.700 --> 14:47.700
-Yes! -Hey, don't just answer me. Sing!

254
14:47.850 --> 14:49.500
I'm warming up my voice!

255
14:49.630 --> 14:51.160
I see. Good. Then I will too.

256
14:51.210 --> 14:56.150
-Ah! -Ah!

257
14:57.750 --> 14:58.810
What are you doing?

258
15:00.640 --> 15:02.240
Have you finally lost it?

259
15:02.650 --> 15:04.890
You're late.

260
15:06.600 --> 15:11.410
I was waiting for you to treat us to jjamppong... Ah!

261
15:11.590 --> 15:13.050
All together! Jjamppong!

262
15:13.080 --> 15:17.270
-Jjamppong... -Ah...

263
15:17.400 --> 15:20.420
[Do not touch.]

264
15:31.340 --> 15:32.870
These coupons still exist?

265
15:34.920 --> 15:37.050
[Junghwa-ru Restaurant coupons]

266
15:36.420 --> 15:37.380
Two, four...

267
15:37.740 --> 15:39.250
Okay, just nice.

268
15:42.110 --> 15:43.130
Okay!

269
15:43.380 --> 15:44.500
Ten coupons give us

270
15:44.770 --> 15:46.210
free pan-fried dumplings.

271
15:46.210 --> 15:47.410
I want jjajangmyeon.

272
15:47.440 --> 15:48.620
I want jjamppong.

273
15:49.700 --> 15:51.050
Jjamppong for me, too.

274
15:51.260 --> 15:52.950
Okay, then.

275
15:53.000 --> 15:54.930
Let's have sweet and sour pork too.

276
15:55.310 --> 15:58.940
One... One jjajangmyeon, (black bean noodles)

277
15:58.950 --> 16:00.750
two jjamppongs, (spicy seafood noodles)

278
16:00.750 --> 16:04.610
and one small sweet and sour pork.

279
16:05.050 --> 16:06.240
Please.

280
16:07.520 --> 16:09.010
Next, stage three.

281
16:07.760 --> 16:10.530
[Training 3: Inject Emotion]

282
16:09.300 --> 16:11.230
Inject emotions into the jajangmyeon.

283
16:11.230 --> 16:12.270
Sorry?

284
16:12.640 --> 16:15.300
You've been in love with someone before, right?

285
16:16.610 --> 16:20.470
Well, try to put some heart-pounding emotion into it. Thump, thump!

286
16:20.600 --> 16:21.930
Aren't we getting food?

287
16:22.400 --> 16:23.370
Too hard?

288
16:23.380 --> 16:25.120
How about emoting the feelings of a breakup?

289
16:25.120 --> 16:27.170
Is that easier to portray?

290
16:29.100 --> 16:31.480
So, a breakup while eating jjajangmyeon?

291
16:31.830 --> 16:33.750
Such great attention to detail.

292
16:33.870 --> 16:35.300
Yes, go with that.

293
16:43.220 --> 16:45.660
One jjajangmyeon,

294
16:45.780 --> 16:47.210
two jjamppongs,

295
16:47.330 --> 16:48.950
and one small sweet and sour pork...

296
16:48.950 --> 16:50.310
Wrong!

297
16:50.590 --> 16:51.720
No...

298
16:51.850 --> 16:55.760
You gave up on the small sweet and sour pork too quickly!

299
16:57.270 --> 17:00.010
Fill the sweet and sour pork with your lingering attachment

300
17:00.010 --> 17:02.190
to the brim.

301
17:06.359 --> 17:09.119
One jjajangmyeon,

302
17:09.260 --> 17:10.530
two jjamppongs,

303
17:10.660 --> 17:13.569
and one small sweet and sour pork.

304
17:14.560 --> 17:15.470
Nice.

305
17:15.680 --> 17:16.940
This time,

306
17:17.329 --> 17:19.180
the delivery arrived,

307
17:19.210 --> 17:20.630
but there's no pickled radish.

308
17:20.630 --> 17:22.780
Like someone having jjajangmyeon without pickled radish,

309
17:22.780 --> 17:24.640
lose yourself in the heartbreak.

310
17:24.760 --> 17:28.530
They absolutely forgot the pickled radish.

311
17:28.910 --> 17:30.310
That one freaking piece

312
17:30.590 --> 17:32.410
of pickled radish.

313
17:35.950 --> 17:38.470
One jjajangmyeon,

314
17:38.590 --> 17:39.950
two jjamppongs,

315
17:40.060 --> 17:42.680
and one small sweet and sour pork.

316
17:42.820 --> 17:43.630
Okay.

317
17:43.760 --> 17:45.220
This time the food arrived,

318
17:45.220 --> 17:47.180
and you didn't opt out of disposables,

319
17:47.180 --> 17:49.240
but they didn't include chopsticks!

320
17:50.720 --> 17:55.230
You have no chopsticks at home,

321
17:55.360 --> 17:56.970
not even wooden ones.

322
17:57.100 --> 17:59.140
None at home at all.

323
17:59.280 --> 18:02.260
You turned the house upside down and still—nothing!

324
18:02.500 --> 18:04.590
You only have your fingers,

325
18:04.810 --> 18:07.150
your dirty fingers.

326
18:08.220 --> 18:10.970
One jjajangmyeon,

327
18:11.100 --> 18:12.720
two jjamppongs,

328
18:12.860 --> 18:14.890
and one small sweet and sour pork.

329
18:17.110 --> 18:18.220
Nice.

330
18:19.610 --> 18:20.930
I'm hungry.

331
18:21.310 --> 18:22.690
Order the food.

332
18:23.200 --> 18:24.200
Okay.

333
18:33.400 --> 18:35.460
Hello, we'd like...

334
18:41.300 --> 18:43.790
One jjajangmyeon,

335
18:43.910 --> 18:45.080
two jjamppongs,

336
18:45.210 --> 18:48.020
and one small sweet and sour pork.

337
18:48.450 --> 18:49.980
Are you freaking serious?

338
18:50.100 --> 18:51.660
Who even makes prank calls

339
18:51.670 --> 18:53.900
these days, you son of a gun!

340
18:54.040 --> 18:55.040
You're mistaken.

341
18:55.180 --> 18:57.020
I just happen to be practicing...

342
18:57.020 --> 18:58.150
Where are you, punk?

343
18:58.230 --> 19:00.460
Huh? Where are you!

344
19:00.660 --> 19:02.350
A singing prank, huh?

345
19:02.530 --> 19:04.790
What did I do to deserve this crap?

346
19:04.960 --> 19:07.420
This little bastard.

347
19:07.620 --> 19:09.750
Gosh, what in the hell was that?

348
19:11.590 --> 19:14.000
He's quite the oddball too.

349
19:14.020 --> 19:14.680
Seriously.

350
19:14.800 --> 19:15.930
Tell me about it.

351
19:16.700 --> 19:18.000
So cute.

352
19:37.100 --> 19:38.190
Thank you.

353
19:41.990 --> 19:42.540
Move.

354
19:42.690 --> 19:43.780
What for?

355
19:44.860 --> 19:46.060
It splatters, right?

356
20:00.260 --> 20:01.600
What the hell?

357
20:03.010 --> 20:04.340
No freaking way!

358
20:05.780 --> 20:07.610
Where's the onion?

359
20:07.620 --> 20:09.570
How is it jjajangmyeon without onion chunks?

360
20:09.570 --> 20:11.000
Damn it!

361
20:11.290 --> 20:12.350
Damn it.

362
20:15.180 --> 20:18.060
[Training 4: Hold Back Your Tears]

363
20:20.050 --> 20:21.100
Peel them.

364
20:24.560 --> 20:25.300
Me?

365
20:25.470 --> 20:27.310
No, both of you.

366
20:27.730 --> 20:29.970
Eh? Why me?

367
20:30.130 --> 20:31.800
Then do you want to go home?

368
20:37.380 --> 20:38.540
So spicy.

369
20:38.780 --> 20:39.880
Sing.

370
20:40.340 --> 20:41.410
Sorry?

371
20:41.540 --> 20:43.230
Start singing now.

372
20:47.100 --> 20:48.560
Can't you see he's crying?

373
20:49.460 --> 20:51.120
Stage four.

374
20:51.320 --> 20:54.930
Even if tears fill your eyes, keep your head up and steady your breath.

375
20:54.930 --> 20:57.800
When tears well up, your throat starts to tighten.

376
20:57.930 --> 21:02.530
Especially for someone like you who has spent their lives swallowing their tears.

377
21:05.810 --> 21:07.480
When is this going to end?

378
21:07.600 --> 21:09.590
Why are you still here? Go home!

379
21:10.480 --> 21:11.900
What about me?

380
21:22.610 --> 21:24.530
This is your home from now on,

381
21:24.710 --> 21:25.910
my dear protégé.

382
21:30.190 --> 21:31.450
Okay.

383
21:33.140 --> 21:34.540
Keep peeling.

384
21:50.960 --> 21:52.100
Again.

385
21:54.000 --> 21:55.570
One more time.

386
22:16.130 --> 22:19.470
The morning meeting has been postponed to 11 AM,

387
22:19.610 --> 22:22.100
followed by what the chairman mentioned...

388
22:24.090 --> 22:25.500
Mr. Lee, are you okay?

389
22:26.720 --> 22:28.400
You don't look so well.

390
22:29.200 --> 22:30.560
I'm tired.

391
22:43.130 --> 22:44.080
Get back to work.

392
22:44.250 --> 22:45.220
Yes.

393
22:48.290 --> 22:50.760
The sound of dawn,

394
22:50.960 --> 22:53.750
my breath calling out to you.

395
22:53.870 --> 22:55.810
I want info on this contestant.

396
22:56.540 --> 22:57.720
Who is he?

397
22:59.530 --> 23:01.070
The person I'm looking for.

398
23:02.110 --> 23:04.530
Since the audition is held by our agency,

399
23:04.790 --> 23:06.190
you should have his info.

400
23:06.300 --> 23:07.330
Yeah?

401
23:09.030 --> 23:11.000
Was there such a contestant?

402
23:12.610 --> 23:15.990
But I can't just disclose his private info.

403
23:16.520 --> 23:17.870
Where is he?

404
23:19.760 --> 23:21.690
Where is Lee Hanyul?

405
23:22.200 --> 23:23.770
Why are you asking me?

406
23:24.990 --> 23:27.060
Stop wasting time and leave.

407
23:31.370 --> 23:34.990
It's not a waste of time. You clearly know where he is!

408
23:37.520 --> 23:39.430
I don't mean your time.

409
23:40.380 --> 23:41.840
You're wasting my time.

410
23:47.550 --> 23:49.210
Get out if you're done asking.

411
24:08.660 --> 24:09.820
Hanyul.

412
24:19.450 --> 24:22.590
I missed you so much, Lee Hanyul.

413
24:33.100 --> 24:36.700
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]
